                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "The game is fun but its way too hard. I'm stuck at the third boss. \n\nEach level has a number of stars you can receive for doing specific achievements. Each star nets you some kind of reward, usually gold, and sometimes a bunch of weapons/armor. The more of the latter you receive, the more you can upgrade, which means you'll need lots of gold to pay for the upgrades.\n\nSo if you want to win, you need to grind out all these stars on each level to have a prayer of defeating the bosses. And wear resistant armor.\n\nThe bosses are incredibly cheap, constantly spawning adds that overwhelm you and basically eliminate your ability to move around, which means you'll never have enough attack/magic points to do any damage. \n\nIf you want to spend an enormous amount of time in each level digging up its secrets, then this might not be a bad game. But these levels can be beat in like 1 minute, with the exit doors shining right in your face from practically the beginning. So if you can ignore that and grind like a mother-f-er, you might enjoy it.",
